#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:5
#: 61fbc327e7c243fa9fc99d40aa1cf7fc
msgid "Copter Mission Command List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:7
#: caa01f638b1d4924b24e45b53e70b7ff
msgid "This page provides details of all the mission commands (i.e. `MAVLink commands <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#MAV_CMD_NAV_WAYPOINT>`__) supported by Copter that can be run as part of a mission (see :ref:`AUTO flight mode <auto-mode>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:10
#: 7a43970d80364f0cbd9552a08e415eb6
msgid "Each of the commands below is either a \"Navigation\" command or a \"Do\" command.  Navigation commands (e.g. \"TakeOff\" and \"Waypoint\") affect the location of the vehicle while \"Do\" commands (e.g. \"Do-Set-Servo\" and \"Do-Cam-Trigg-Dist\") are for auxiliary functions and do not affect the vehicle's position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:14
#: c9d5cb04810a44099b324aba521534ef
msgid "During a mission at most one \"Navigation\" command and one \"Do\" command can be running at one time.  The \"Do\" commands will be run in order as soon as the preceding navigation command before them completes.  For more information on setting up missions please refer to the :ref:`Planning a Mission with Waypoints and Events <common-planning-a-mission-with-waypoints-and-events>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:19
#: 2727234a8465435e9d990e87b575c32d
msgid "Takeoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:24
#: b596ec0f3db548f89b92454b0882d083
msgid "The vehicle will climb straight up from its current location to the altitude specified (in meters). This should be the first command of nearly all missions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:28
#: b025ff51dc31413db9f9774a1d5e63e6
msgid "If the mission is begun while the copter is already flying, the vehicle will climb straight up to the specified altitude, if the vehicle is already above the specified altitude the takeoff command will be ignored and the mission will move onto the next command immediately.  In this case any \"DO\" commands immediately following the TAKEOFF will also be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:35
#: 50c8dde482264ed5af1123222f99feaa
msgid "Waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:40
#: e9dccc2f923e4d5d99fbc0b8fce01f1c
msgid "The vehicle will fly a straight line to the location specified as a lat, lon and altitude (in meters)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:43
#: 9f620b9eef49492b9a77c596374cf639
msgid "**Delay** - the amount of time to wait (in seconds) at the waypoint before proceeding to the next command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:46
#: 450d1caa9ca241fc979a5661f9b6aeec
msgid "**Hit Rad** - not supported - meant to hold the distance (in meters) from the target point that will qualify the waypoint as complete. This command is not supported. Instead, the :ref:`WP_RADIUS_M<WP_RADIUS_M>` parameter should be used (see \"WP Radius\" field in the above screenshot or adjust through the Standard Parameters List).  Even the :ref:`WP_RADIUS_M<WP_RADIUS_M>` is only used when the waypoint has a Delay. With no delay specified the waypoint will be considered complete when the virtual point that the vehicle is chasing reaches the waypoint. This can be 10m (or more) ahead of the vehicle meaning that the vehicle will turn towards the following waypoint long before it actually reaches the current waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:57
#: e42e83d3b5af45c4a91eee52dca30686
msgid "**Yaw Ang** - not supported - meant to hold the resulting yaw angle in degrees (0=north, 90 = east). Instead use a :ref:`CONDITION_YAW <mission-command-list_condition-yaw>` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:61
#: a758a326f2474b92bb66ed256fa66df3
msgid "**Lat, Lon** - the latitude and longitude targets.  If left as zero, current location will be substituted for waypoint location, making it appear as if the waypoint is simply skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:63
#: 081f015ab4d140faaa76c2571598f2ae
msgid "**Alt** - the target altitude above home in meters.  If left as zero it will hold the current altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:67
#: 119c6871af424feeb98508f841f8ded2
msgid "Spline Waypoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:72
#: 43408c9090f94a4e90f2976ec49ab83e
msgid "`Spline <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spline_%28mathematics%29>`__ waypoints take all the same arguments as regular waypoints (lat, lon, alt, delay) but when executed the vehicle will fly smooth paths (both vertically and horizontally) instead of straight lines.  Spline waypoints can be mixed with regular straight line waypoints as shown in the image above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:74
#: c1948da2a6a94d9ba90f72f3533e2773
msgid "The Mission Planner shows the path the vehicle will take.  The image above shows some characteristics of the spline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:77
#: 4230d3e4503149768346b774f4d24874
msgid "The 1 second delay at the end of Waypoint #1 causes the vehicle to stop so Spline command #2 begins by taking a sharp 90degree turn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:79
#: 575f6249b8a2448880a9134ce6c7a98a
msgid "The direction of travel as the vehicle passes through Spline Waypoint #3 is parallel to an imaginary line drawn between waypoints #2 and #4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:81
#: b8d79b9dd4cc407883fcc890be4c8ec4
msgid "Waypoint #5 is a straight line so the vehicle lines itself up to point towards waypoint #5 even before reaching waypoint #4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:85
#: 0e3e73bbb3714d92af277dfbf118c55d
msgid "Loiter_Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:90
#: 687fef68f1104614a04f094ae6497ca2
msgid "The vehicle will fly to and then wait at the specified location for the specified number of seconds.  This is the same as a Waypoint command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:93
#: 488845d569eb44d0a50a60fafe360625
msgid "**Times** - the number of seconds to remain at the location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:95
#: 44aa898d9c09461ca3199fc8684bf009
msgid "**Lat, Lon** - the latitude and longitude targets. If left as zero it will hold at the current location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:98
#: 00383f3852e04c638df0d9899ab3130f
msgid "**Alt** - the target altitude above home in meters. If left as zero it will hold at the current altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:102
#: 279f550153c14a6c9429d644afdd5214
msgid "Loiter_Turns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:107
#: 87bee03d75da458298a3a6a35bed9e2c
msgid "The mission equivalent of the :ref:`Circle flight mode <circle-mode>`.  Loiter (circle) the specified location for at least the specified number of complete turns, and then proceed to the next command upon intersection of the course to it with the circle's perimeter. If zero is specified for a latitude/longitude/altitude parameter then the current location value for the parameter will be used. Fractional turns between 0 and 1 are supported, while turns greater than 1 must be integers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:111
#: 5c209a4bda7946e7829ac1dfec9e4ecd
msgid "The radius of the circle is controlled by the command parameter. A radius of 0 will result in the copter loitering at the location and pirouetting the specified number of turns. Negative radius values result in counter-clockwise turns instead of clockwise turns. Radius values over 255 meters will be rounded down to the nearest 10 meter mark ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:114
#: 43717bb2de4d4109950527914560b024
msgid "**Turn** - the number of full rotations to complete around the point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:116
#: 809935df830d473f9d46d596fe351d34
msgid "Fractional turns between 0 and 1 are supported, while turns greater than 1 must be integers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:118
#: e92d1f2d653a4842bf79a4dcb7aaa365
msgid "**Radius** - Loiter radius around waypoint. Units are in meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:120
#: ff376cfde704470da712182a9cd67667
msgid "**Lat, Lon** - the latitude and longitude targets.  If left as zero it will circle around the current location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:123
#: c2e8e216a47d43ee8ee91aba9a081dc5
msgid "**Alt** - the target altitude above home in meters.  If left as zero it will circle at the current altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:127
#: 4020c0fb79ed4796a29430a673961836
msgid "Loiter_Unlimited"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:132
#: c1ac65a166434d79ac41c53faaad58b4
msgid "The vehicle will fly to and then wait at the specified location indefinitely.  The mission will not proceed past this command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:135
#: 29e6aa8668114580a1d6a2698501be29
msgid "**Lat, Lon** - the latitude and longitude targets. If left as zero it will wait at the current location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:138
#: 42a5267f7fd348da97c095637e3bb560
msgid "**Alt** - the target altitude above home in meters. If left as zero it will wait at the current altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:142
#: e619f67c9d0e49079ee237a54fe3a0e1
msgid "Return-To-Launch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:147
#: 20b1febf749347a5b57dd5a513290608
msgid "Mission equivalent of the :ref:`RTL flight mode <rtl-mode>`.  As described on the RTL flight mode wiki page, the vehicle will first climb to the :ref:`RTL_ALT_M<RTL_ALT_M>` parameter's specified altitude (default is 15m) before returning home.  The home location is where the vehicle was last armed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:152
#: 6fa45ef52c134a01a6583f2a9c01ebe6
msgid "This command takes no parameters and generally should be the last command in the mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:156
#: 234656d41a4e48379c28deeead531d82
msgid "Land"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:161
#: a56a6aadbbbf467da7b6fdf58b146bfa
msgid "The vehicle will land at its current location or at the lat/lon coordinates provided.  This is the mission equivalent of the :ref:`LAND flight mode <land-mode>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:164
#: 69d49641429141759b8c463ba609b4bf
msgid "**Lat, Lon** - the latitude and longitude targets. If left as zero it will land at the current location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:168
#: 04c5441b53734c618d10b5405054a982
msgid "Delay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:173
#: 8ea4e5ca8a6b484596f9b68907504435
msgid "The vehicle will remain at its current location until the specified number of seconds has passed or the absolute time is reached. The first column (\"Seconds\") holds the number of seconds to delay.  Set to -1 if this field should be ignored. The \"hour UTC\", \"minute UTC\" and \"second UTC\" fields can be used to specify an absolute time (`UTC <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coordinated_Universal_Time>`__).  The example above will cause the vehicle to take-off at 1:30pm UTC.  Note that the hour and/or minute field can also be ignored by setting them to -1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:177
#: 9afdbf37f05a40a9ba5fec4e496b1c44
msgid "This is a video made during the development of this feature.  Note in the video CONDITION_DELAY command is used but in its final version, this DELAY command should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:183
#: fb8a9fe2b3cc4d0c88e180e3d9b8dbea
msgid "Payload Place"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:188
#: 81924330ce5b46e7814e88db5a7a874d
msgid "The vehicle flies to the specified location and descends until it senses (using motor output) that the package has reached the ground.  The gripper is then released to unload the package and ascend back to the waypoint altitude. The first column (\"Max Desc\") holds the maximum descent (in meters) that the vehicle should descend.  If the package has still not reached the ground despite this descent, the package will not be released and the vehicle will return to  the waypoint altitude and advance to the next mission command. Parameters controlling this operation (besides :ref:`Gripper parameters <common-gripper-landingpage>`) are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:192
#: 839c99ef7080448ba5c44d12fae05b88
msgid ":ref:`PLDP_SPEED_DN<PLDP_SPEED_DN>`: Descent speed, once the waypoint is reached, is either :ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>` or this value, if non-zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:193
#: b50f2511125e490ca2dd01801e05cff3
msgid ":ref:`PLDP_THRESH<PLDP_THRESH>`: The percentage of thrust decrease that indicates payload touch-down. The reference thrust is measured over the first two seconds of descent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:194
#: 1d57a29d1cf249a9a08056275e69d0c2
msgid ":ref:`PLDP_RNG_MAX<PLDP_RNG_MAX>`: If non-zero, the maximum release height over ground obtained from a downward facing rangerfinder. Automatic gripper release can occur only if below this altitude above ground in addition to thrust reduction being obtained. If this value is non zero and no rangefinder is present, the place will be aborted and the vehicle will ascend and proceed to the next waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:195
#: 86f90e54f85f4fc0a99c24d73cc9de4e
msgid ":ref:`PLDP_DELAY<PLDP_DELAY>`: Delay in seconds after release the vehicle will remain in position after release before ascending. This allows payload replacement if the gripper is set to re-engage after a delay (see :ref:`GRIP_AUTOCLOSE<GRIP_AUTOCLOSE>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:201
#: 8801347924ae490897fa9b739ec98c7d
msgid "Attitude Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:206
#: d9e2c266bd7f4adbac9a4bdfcfff2244
msgid "Vehicle maintains the specified roll, pitch, yaw angle and climb rate for the specified time.  GPS is not required while this command is being executed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:208
#: 142c99404feb42f29e3fb02baa26a51e
msgid "**Roll**: positive is lean right, negative is lean left"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:209
#: b2f1e3811326419b9ff91a93ba1573e1
msgid "**Pitch**: positive is lean back, negative is lean forward"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:210
#: 7cb2410c003a4265abc584d2e8a8a0b4
msgid "**Yaw**: 0 is North, 90 is East, 180 is South, 270 is West"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:211
#: 725f1582ff894d938ee52e70c164f61d
msgid "**ClimbRate**: in m/s but most ground stations incorrectly scale this parameter so it is best to leave at 0m/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:217
#: 275988d3e527471aabfec332a0ea47a1
msgid "Script Time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:222
#: 60f614b51fee4083a452f9ead74245ce
msgid "Lua script runs for the specified time after which it will move onto the next command.  \"command\", \"arg1\" and \"arg2\" arguments are interpreted by the script. The demonstration below used this SCRIPT_TIME command to execute the \"fast descent\" script from within Auto mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:231
#: dcf3efac48e849be8b852bf88e9f9b4f
msgid "Do-Set-ROI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:236
#: fd8dc169eeaf4480b71373995eee4302
msgid "Points the nose of the vehicle or :ref:`camera gimbal <common-cameras-and-gimbals>` at the \"region of interest\".  In the example above the nose or camera would be pointed at the red marker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:238
#: b7ece5e282af4e9fb1937d7799070417
msgid "The nose will continue to point at the red marker until the end of the mission OR \"clear\" the do-set-roi and cause the vehicle to return to its default behaviour (i.e. pointing at the next waypoint) by adding a second DO_SET_ROI command later in the mission with all zero for Lat, Lon, and Alt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:240
#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:359
#: 5e0ac254b8304227ba6b71fba51a7fc3
#: 1be15fa8e0b04e63aedd8f07beda0355
msgid "**Lat, Lon** - the latitude and longitude targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:242
#: c13ea2cffe51471b8c3c60c11e7b207f
msgid "**Alt** - the target altitude above home in meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:248
#: 4c8c31566bd0470bb069124c9246924d
msgid "Condition-Delay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:253
#: 653bbad0aab340cb839442bd1be64a6d
msgid "Delays the start of the next \"Do\" command for the specified number of seconds. In the example above, Command #4 (Do-Set-Roi) is delayed so that it only starts 5 seconds after the vehicle has passed Waypoint #2. Note: this command does not stop the vehicle. Also note that the delay timer is only active until the next waypoint is reached, so if the \"Do\" command hasn't been triggered by then it never will be."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:260
#: 59cc059c0dda446a9189cca8daeaeebc
msgid "**Time (sec)** - the time to delay the next \"Do\" command in seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:263
#: 375451d8d5d74fe4a3a3d294f72a1568
msgid "Condition-Distance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:268
#: 58764a080e174d5c87c4e55b46e8a2fe
msgid "Delays the start of the next \"Do\" command until the vehicle is within the specified number of meters of the next waypoint. In the example above, Command #4 (Do-Set-Roi) is delayed so that it only starts once the vehicle is within 50m of waypoint #5. Note: this command does not cause the vehicle to stop or pause during the mission, it only affects \"Do\" commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:275
#: 3608706730c64f6baa41628926b48c1d
msgid "**Dist (m)** - how close the vehicle should be to the next waypoint (in meters) before beginning the next \"Do\" command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:282
#: f2c7791c329e4631945c64bcfec6f159
msgid "Condition-Yaw"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:287
#: 28bb8616741a4fdca1477788db755419
msgid "Point the nose of the vehicle to the specified heading by a specified amount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:290
#: 9aece6ea473440b49bf88a74493eacda
msgid "**Deg** - the desired heading in degrees (0 = North, 90 = East, etc) when \"rel/abs\" field is \"0\" (meaning absolute)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:293
#: 1d62ec672d4944e88e44c38e46ec022f
msgid "OR the change in heading (in degrees) when \"rel/abs\" field is \"1\" (meaning relative)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:296
#: d0dbcb1330584ed09a9c30f2c3cf1dad
msgid "**Speed deg/s** - the rotation speed (in deg/sec) as the vehicle turns to the desired heading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:299
#: f39cc8737b854b18b5ab0d1e1888ef2c
msgid "**Dir 1=CW** - Used to denote the direction of rotation to achieve the target angle (1=CW, -1=CCW, 0= the vehicle will always turn in direction that most quickly gets it to the new target heading, but only when \"rel/abs\" = \"0\",)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:301
#: d6de81278e374547abadaef0d3c67629
msgid "**rel/abs (0=Abs, 1=Rel)** - allows specifying the heading (i.e \"Deg\" field) as an absolute heading (if \"0\") or relative to the current heading (if \"1\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:305
#: 3929ff079fef4fabbd7193e4073a2f22
msgid "Do-Jump"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:310
#: 9034459004784033ba4bb5c324898c72
msgid "Jump to the specified mission command the specified number of times before continuing with the mission.  In the example above the vehicle would fly back-and-forth between waypoints #1 and #2 a total of 3 times before flying on to waypoint #4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:315
#: c2ee603dcc19468db033604e8f7be859
msgid "**WP #** - the mission command to jump to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:317
#: 8347efd29df840ecb0cc03b8faaddd81
msgid "**Repeat** - the maximum number of times we should perform the jump. -1 means always jump"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:320
#: 119fde7c68574f49b09e38ca4a43c746
msgid "Despite the name, Do-Jump is really a \"Nav\" command rather than a \"Do\" command, so conditional commands like CONDITION_DELAY won't affect Do-Jump, it will always perform the jump as soon as it hits that command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:327
#: a61cb1002e65477f95426d9c44377884
msgid "No more that one hundred (100) Do-Jump commands can be used in a mission. This value is further reduced to fifteen (15) Do-Jump commands for boards with less than 500kb of ram. Subsequent Do-Jumps will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:330
#: dc449dfe0ce54dcab4766982e0adfc42
msgid "Do-Aux-Function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:335
#: 1caaf0e49fc84d488a46995075240246
msgid "Allows any :ref:`auxiliary function <common-auxiliary-functions>` to be executed from within a mission without setting up an auxiliary switch.  The \"AuxFunction\" field should be set to the \"RCx_OPTION value\" from the linked page.  The \"Switch\" fields corresponds to the auxiliary function switch position with \"0\" meaning \"low\", \"1\" meaning \"middle\" and \"2\" meaning high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:338
#: c14ff6407c1642b9991e177e53f832b6
msgid "Do-Change-Speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:343
#: 5c79cf530177450d889400169d72713c
msgid "Change the desired maximum speed (in meters/sec) of the vehicle.  Normally the \"Type\" field is left at 0 meaning the horizontal speed is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:345
#: 85ba916d22a84542a9851b6833f4b0da
msgid "**Type** - 0,1:ground speed, 2:climb rate, 3:descent rate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:347
#: f5a8f44b49ea4301bd482cc9f0665b4a
msgid "**Speed m/s** - the desired maximum speed in meters/second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:350
#: 2efae77cc8224dba81b1dcc2bb5920e7
msgid "Do-Set-Home"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:355
#: d12b60718043474c810487c8907b5e85
msgid "This command should be avoided if possible and instead use :ref:`Rally Points <common-rally-points>` which can also control the position used for Return-To-Launch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:357
#: 3fb595e1c76e42ef9214dff8921895a4
msgid "**Current(1)/Spec(0)** - if \"1\" use the current location as the new home, if \"0\" use the specified Lat and Lon coordinate (not labelled yet!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:362
#: 41f5f695ad6c4b1586386518680507b3
msgid "Do-Set-Cam-Trigg-Dist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-command-list.rst:367
#: 4643ab9fc0b84ae5ba1061a5af4c9ca0
msgid "Trigger the :ref:`camera shutter <common-camera-shutter-with-servo>` at regular distance intervals. For example the command above will cause the camera shutter to trigger after every 5m that the vehicle travels."
msgstr ""

